    "result": "I implemented `parse_line` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`. I haven't run or tested it, since shell access wasn't available.\n\nIt checks the argument types and separator first, raising `TypeError` or `ValueError` as specified. It then scans the line field by field. A field starting with `\"` is read as quoted, with `\"\"` becoming one `\"`. After the closing quote, only `sep` or the end of the line is allowed. An unquoted field is read up to the next `sep`. A `\"`, `\\r` or `\\n` inside an unquoted field raises `ValueError`, and so does a quoted field with no closing quote. A trailing `sep` produces a final empty field, so `\"a,\"` gives `[\"a\", \"\"]`.",
